{"skill":{"slug":"n8n-automation","displayName":"n8n Automation"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769873640669,"changelog":"Initial release of n8n-automation skill.\n\n- Control and manage n8n workflows via the n8n REST API.\n- Supports listing, creating, activating/deactivating, triggering, and debugging workflows.\n- Compatible with both n8n Cloud and self-hosted instances.\n- Includes setup instructions, command-line API usage examples, and common automation patterns.\n- Provides quick references for workflow and execution management tasks.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3816,"sha256":"6a676c36ad2c6963b238a0f3659a08ece0b29b994656c42e3eeee746e2bc9e8a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/api-endpoints.md","size":2350,"sha256":"77d00e4a930ca66a1c88a1cb86eaacc2b1d006ded7c8ebfec3cbbade9f8581d4","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1914,"sha256":"0a3521ba936c30a981d21e387f57d77ff388247f8111d6543777a9a350596c87","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024866714,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"78a6a95be4278a7d218db1bd2683c4eae045a3a6a11475ba0990b7c701f79d6d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/78a6a95be4278a7d218db1bd2683c4eae045a3a6a11475ba0990b7c701f79d6d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: n8n-automation\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to manage n8n workflows via its REST API, which is clearly stated in SKILL.md. All provided `curl` commands interact with the user-configured n8n API endpoint using an API key, which is necessary for its functionality. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution (e.g., `curl|bash` of unknown remote payloads), persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent to perform actions outside the stated purpose. The `references/api-endpoints.md` further clarifies the API's scope, including that credential secrets are not exposed via the API, reinforcing the benign nature of the skill's intended use.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160479064},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":34,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789024866714},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a straightforward n8n API helper, but it includes live production triggers and destructive admin actions without enough scoping or confirmation guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill asks for an n8n API URL and API key and notes that the key may have full access on non-enterprise plans; that level of authority can be proportionate for administration, but the skill does not sufficiently constrain destructive or live-production use.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is markdown-only, has no executable files, dependency installation, background setup, or installer behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions provide direct curl commands for production webhooks and DELETE operations without warning that these can execute live automations or remove production resources, and without requiring explicit user confirmation or backup steps.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No local persistence, services, memory writes, or privilege escalation were found, but the API credentials it uses may grant persistent remote administrative access to the configured n8n instance.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Managing n8n workflows is coherent with the stated purpose, but the documented capabilities include deleting workflows and reference endpoints for deleting credentials, executions, tags, and transferring workflow ownership, which are high-impact actions not fully reflected in the manifest description.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to let the agent administer an n8n instance. Use a least-privilege API key where possible, prefer test webhooks before production webhooks, and require explicit confirmation and backups before any delete, deactivate, transfer, or credential-related action.","findings":"[E1] expected: The external transmissions are calls to the user-configured n8n API and are expected for a REST API management skill, not evidence of unrelated exfiltration.\n[E1] expected: Execution-listing API calls send requests to the configured n8n endpoint and fit the debugging and monitoring purpose, though users should avoid exposing sensitive execution data unnecessarily.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The production webhook example can trigger live automations and transmit payloads to connected systems, but the skill does not warn users to prefer test webhooks or confirm production side effects first.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The Delete Workflow command is documented in the body but omitted from the manifest capability summary, creating a scope mismatch for a destructive action.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The workflow deletion command is provided without explicit confirmation, backup, or safer-alternative guidance.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The endpoint reference lists destructive and admin-sensitive endpoints, including delete and transfer operations, without warnings or containment guidance.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024866714}}}}}